{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099245-help-a-new-guy","id":1099245,"title":"Help a new guy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-01T12:33:01-07:00","id":1099245,"title":"Help a new guy","content":"Hey all! For some time now I've been trying to find a stable game with no luck. I honestly don't know where to search anymore. Does anyone know where I can find groups to play the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11086-capt0skittles","name":"capt0skittles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:21:30-07:00","id":1099288,"title":"","content":"In person? Kind of hard to give good advice because it varies a lot from place to place. It might be worth checking out local colleges/universities, gaming stores (don't have to be RPG focused ones), and such places to see if you can find any people nearby.<br /> <br /> If you're willing to branch into online based play, there's a subforum here for it, and you can look at places like roll20 for games open to new recruits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T07:32:32-07:00","id":1099511,"title":"","content":"Maybe try a gaming association and, if you are ready to be the storyteller, propose to game master an RPG","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:58:03-07:00","id":1099537,"title":"","content":"The hardest part of getting into gaming. I strongly suggest just going for friends, potentially family. Gaming stores tend to have some method to connect with others, and the internet has other ways through Meet Ups and stuff like that. If you're in college, odds are there's a club somewhere on campus that's devoted to games where you might find others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}